<!--
  Atm.Protocol.csproj - The shared language of the two machines.

  Why this project exists as its own library: the terminal and the host must agree,
  byte for byte, on what a message looks like. If each side defined its own copy of
  the message types, the two copies would drift and the bug would only show up on
  the wire, at the worst possible moment. One project, referenced by both sides,
  makes disagreement impossible to compile.

  It references nothing. It must stay that way: the contract may not depend on
  either side's implementation.
-->
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
</Project>
